---
layout: base.njk
title: "Private Water Supplies | Bespoke Borehole Systems | Invicta Water Treatment"
description: "Design, install and servicing of bespoke private water supplies for landed estates and premium properties across Surrey, Sussex and the South East. UKAS-accredited testing, 24hr callout."
canonical: "https://www.invictawatertreatment.co.uk/"
permalink: "/"
current: "home"
extraStyles: ["home"]
---
    <!-- ===================== HERO =====================================
      The ReoGreen arrangement: a calm cream field carrying only the eyebrow,
      the headline and two buttons, and the photograph sitting underneath it
      full width, cropped so its subject lands low in the frame. The first
      screen is nearly all air, which is the point — nothing competes with the
      headline, and the picture arrives as a reveal rather than as a backdrop.

      Four things, and no paragraph. The lead that used to sit here ("bespoke
      borehole and spring systems...") is said properly in the section below,
      and the "who we work for" rail is said again in full in the sectors band:
      both were a second and third read competing with the one line that
      matters. What is left is the positioning line, the headline, and the two
      things you can do.
    -->
    <section class="home-hero section--light">
      <div class="container home-hero__inner">
        <p class="eyebrow home-hero__eyebrow">Private water supplies<br>Surrey &amp; Sussex</p>
        <h1 class="home-hero__title">
          Independent water,<br>
          <span class="em">designed around your source.</span>
        </h1>
        <div class="home-hero__actions">
          <a class="btn-inquiry btn-inquiry--lg" href="/enquiry/">Send enquiry <span class="btn-inquiry__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a>
          <a class="btn-line btn-line--lg" href="/services/private-water-supplies/">Private water supplies</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="home-hero__media">
        <img src="/assets/estate-dawn.webp" alt="A country estate at dawn, mist settling across the parkland below the house." fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== ABOUT + USPs (white) ===================== -->
    <section class="section section--paper home-about" aria-labelledby="home-about-title">
      <div class="container home-about__grid">
        <div class="home-about__body">
          <h2 id="home-about-title" class="statement home-about__title">
            Twenty years of private supplies,
            <span class="em">designed for the property, not the price list.</span>
          </h2>
          <p class="home-about__lead">
            Every source is different, and doing it properly is not a job for generalists. We survey
            the water before anything is specified, design the treatment around what we find, and
            install it with our own engineers rather than subcontractors. The same people who built
            your system are the ones who come back to service it.
          </p>

          <ul class="usps" role="list">
            <li class="usp">
              <span class="usp__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3v18M5 10c0 3.9 3.1 7 7 7s7-3.1 7-7"/><path d="M8 6l4-3 4 3"/></svg>
              </span>
              <p class="usp__figure">20+</p>
              <h3 class="usp__label">Years serving the South East</h3>
            </li>
            <li class="usp">
              <span class="usp__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3.5 2"/></svg>
              </span>
              <p class="usp__figure">24h</p>
              <h3 class="usp__label">Emergency response, no call centre</h3>
            </li>
            <li class="usp">
              <span class="usp__icon" aria-hidden="true">
                <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 12.5l5 5 11-11"/></svg>
              </span>
              <p class="usp__figure">UKAS</p>
              <h3 class="usp__label">Accredited testing, to source</h3>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== SERVICES AS CARDS (cream) ===================== -->
    <section class="section section--light home-services" aria-labelledby="home-services-title">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 id="home-services-title" class="statement home-services__title">
          Four services, <span class="em">one team behind all of them.</span>
        </h2>

        <ul class="svc-cards" role="list">
          {% for s in site.services %}
          <li class="svc-cards__item">
            <a class="svc-card" href="{{ s.href }}">
              <span class="svc-card__index">({{ "0" + loop.index }})</span>
              <h3 class="svc-card__title">{{ s.title }}</h3>
              <p class="svc-card__desc">{{ s.desc }}</p>
              <span class="svc-card__cta">
                Explore
                <span class="svc-card__arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== HOW WE WORK (dark, stacking cards) =====================
      The cards are position:sticky at the same offset, so each one comes to rest
      under the header and the next slides over the top of it. Offsetting the rest
      position by index leaves a sliver of the card beneath showing, which is what
      makes it read as a stack rather than a single swap.
    -->
    {% set steps = [
      { title: "Site survey & water analysis",
        copy: "Every supply starts with a survey and a UKAS-accredited analysis. Nothing is specified before we know the flow rate, the depth and the full chemistry of what is coming out of the ground.",
        img: "/assets/service-water-hygiene.webp",
        alt: "Labelled sample bottles from a day's testing lined up on a laboratory bench beside the results sheet." },
      { title: "Bespoke system design",
        copy: "Filtration, storage and pumping designed to match your source and your property's demand. Everything specified is chosen for reliability and long service life.",
        img: "/assets/step-design.webp",
        alt: "Architectural floor-plan and elevation drawings with a pen and brass ruler." },
      { title: "Filtration & treatment",
        copy: "Treatment built around your water's chemistry: iron and manganese reduction, pH correction, and UV sterilisation where it is needed. Treated to a standard mains water rarely matches.",
        img: "/assets/step-treatment.webp",
        alt: "A plant room with a treatment vessel and copper pipework manifold." },
      { title: "Installation",
        copy: "Our own engineers install every system, never subcontracted. The plant is set out cleanly, commissioned properly, and left in a state we would be happy to return to in ten years.",
        img: "/assets/step-install.webp",
        alt: "An estate plant room in a stone outbuilding, with cylinder and copper pipework." },
      { title: "Servicing & maintenance",
        copy: "Planned visits keep the system at spec, with annual UKAS re-testing. Service clients reach our engineers directly on the 24-hour line: same number, same team, no call centre.",
        img: "/assets/service-servicing.webp",
        alt: "An Invicta van on the drive of a period property, with the borehole chamber open and the pump and rising main lifted out." }
    ] %}
    <section class="section home-process" aria-labelledby="home-process-title">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 id="home-process-title" class="statement home-process__title">
          From first survey <span class="em">to final commissioning.</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="stack">
          {% for st in steps %}
          <article class="stack__card" style="--i: {{ loop.index0 }}">
            <div class="stack__text">
              <span class="numeral numeral--sm stack__index" aria-hidden="true">{{ "0" + loop.index }}</span>
              <h3 class="stack__title">{{ st.title }}</h3>
              <p class="stack__copy">{{ st.copy }}</p>
              <a class="btn-line stack__cta" href="/enquiry/">Send enquiry</a>
            </div>
            <div class="stack__media">
              <img src="{{ st.img }}" alt="{{ st.alt }}" loading="lazy">
            </div>
          </article>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== SELECTED WORK (white) =====================
      Hand-picked for the home page rather than filtered by service: the
      flagship, the National Trust name, and the one that best shows what we
      build ourselves. Same component as the service pages.
    -->
    {% set homePicks = ["lk-effingham", "uppark-sussex", "u-farm-kent"] %}
    {% set studies = [] %}
    {% for id in homePicks %}{% for cs in caseStudies %}{% if cs.id == id %}{% set _ = studies.push(cs) %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endfor %}
    {% set carouselId = "home" %}
    {% set carouselSurface = "section--paper" %}
    {% set carouselTitle = "Supplies we've designed, <span class='em'>installed and looked after.</span>" %}
    {% set carouselLead = "A National Trust restoration, a multi-source estate system, and a membrane plant we built ourselves. Step through to see the work." %}
    {% include "case-carousel.njk" %}

    <!-- ===================== TRUSTED BY (cream) ===================== -->
    <section class="section section--light clients home-clients" aria-labelledby="home-clients-title">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 id="home-clients-title" class="statement">
          Chosen by clients who <span class="em">expect it done properly.</span>
        </h2>

        <ul class="clients__grid">
          <li class="client"><span>Chelsea FC</span></li>
          <li class="client"><span>GSK</span></li>
          <li class="client"><span>Amgen</span></li>
          <li class="client"><span>Cowdray Estate</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== REVIEWS (white) ===================== -->
    <section class="section section--paper home-reviews" aria-labelledby="home-reviews-title">
      <div class="container">
        <h2 id="home-reviews-title" class="statement home-reviews__title">
          What clients say <span class="em">once the water is running.</span>
        </h2>

        <ul class="reviews" role="list">
          {% if testimonials and testimonials.length %}
          {% for t in testimonials %}
          <li class="review{% if t.placeholder %} review--sample{% endif %}">
            <span class="review__mark" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M9.5 5C6.5 6.6 4.8 9.3 4.8 12.5V19h6.4v-6.4H8c0-2 .9-3.6 2.8-4.8L9.5 5zm9 0c-3 1.6-4.7 4.3-4.7 7.5V19h6.4v-6.4H17c0-2 .9-3.6 2.8-4.8L18.5 5z"/></svg>
            </span>
            {# The chip is the safety catch on written samples: it ships with the
               words, so invented praise cannot pass as a real client by anyone
               forgetting about _data/testimonials.js. Drop `placeholder: true`
               from a review when the real one replaces it. #}
            {% if t.placeholder %}<p class="review__flag">Sample copy, not a real client</p>{% endif %}
            <blockquote class="review__quote">{{ t.quote }}</blockquote>
            <p class="review__by">{{ t.name }}<span>{{ t.role }}</span></p>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
          {% else %}
          {# No invented praise: real quotes only. Placeholders hold the layout
             until Stefan supplies them, in the same house style as the
             "photo to follow" blocks. See _data/testimonials.js. #}
          {% for i in [1, 2, 3, 4] %}
          <li class="review review--empty">
            <span class="review__mark" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path d="M9.5 5C6.5 6.6 4.8 9.3 4.8 12.5V19h6.4v-6.4H8c0-2 .9-3.6 2.8-4.8L9.5 5zm9 0c-3 1.6-4.7 4.3-4.7 7.5V19h6.4v-6.4H17c0-2 .9-3.6 2.8-4.8L18.5 5z"/></svg>
            </span>
            <p class="review__placeholder">Client quote to follow</p>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
          {% endif %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== FAQ (dark) =====================
      The five questions we are asked before anything else. Answers are the same
      ones given in full on the private water supplies page, not new claims.
    -->
    {% set homeFaqs = [
      { q: "Do I need permission to install a borehole?",
        a: "In most cases, no formal planning permission is required, though water abstraction over 20 cubic metres per day requires a licence from the Environment Agency. We handle the paperwork and liaison as part of any install where it's needed." },
      { q: "How long does a borehole and treatment system last?",
        a: "A properly designed and installed system will run for 25 to 40 years with routine maintenance. Filtration media and UV lamps are consumables replaced on a service schedule. The borehole itself, the pump housing and the treatment vessels are all long-life." },
      { q: "Can you take over a system installed by someone else?",
        a: "Yes, provided the system is safe to work on and we can access the plant. We start with a full inspection and water analysis, then propose any remedial work needed before taking on the ongoing service contract." },
      { q: "What happens if something goes wrong outside working hours?",
        a: "Existing service clients have direct access to our engineers on a 24-hour emergency line. In most cases we can get to site within four hours of the call." },
      { q: "What does a typical install cost?",
        a: "Every install is bespoke, so there is no typical figure. Costs depend on source depth, water chemistry, storage requirements and property demand. We provide a fixed-price quote after a site survey." }
    ] %}
    <section class="section faq" aria-labelledby="home-faq-title">
      <div class="container faq__grid">
        <aside class="faq__aside">
          <h2 id="home-faq-title" class="faq__title">Frequently asked.</h2>
          <p class="faq__intro">The questions we hear most often from clients thinking about a private supply. If yours isn't answered here, get in touch, we'll answer plainly.</p>
        </aside>

        <div class="faq__list">
          {% for f in homeFaqs %}
          <details class="faq__item">
            <summary class="faq__q">
              {{ f.q }}
              <svg class="faq__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/></svg>
            </summary>
            <p class="faq__a">{{ f.a }}</p>
          </details>
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
